    {
      "output": "The command did not return any output, which suggests that the GitHub releases page may not be structured in a way that allows direct extraction of the download URL using simple `curl` and `grep`. \n\nAs an alternative, I recommend visiting the [Harbor GitHub Releases page](https://github.com/goharbor/harbor/releases/latest) manually. From there, you can:\n\n1. Navigate to the \"Assets\" section.\n2. Look for the installer files, such as:\n   - `harbor-offline-installer-<version>.tgz` (for offline installation)\n   - `harbor-online-installer-<version>.tgz` (for online installation)\n\nThe exact URL will depend on the latest version of Harbor. For example, if the latest version is `v2.8.0`, the installer URL might be:\n\n```\nhttps://github.com/goharbor/harbor/releases/download/v2.8.0/harbor-offline-installer-v2.8.0.tgz\n```\n\nIf you need the exact URL for automation or further assistance, let me know, and I can help you fetch it programmatically or guide you on how to do so.\n",
